  {%- if template == 'page.home-v2' or template == 'page.home-page-speed' -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      ===========================================================================
      Wave B Part 5 — Content-Security-Policy meta tag (script-src restriction)
      Added 2026-04-27. Blocks 6 app-embed <script src> tags that Shopify's
      app-embed pipeline injects just before </head> (Atomato, Bevy Share Cart,
      Gang-sheet, Apploy primary, Intercom primary, Yotpo Reviews + Loyalty).
      ===========================================================================
      Why CSP and not appendChild monkey-patch:
        Those 6 apps are injected as static <script src> tags by the HTML
        parser, not via JS calling appendChild. The parser bypasses any
        Node.prototype.appendChild override. CSP script-src enforcement runs
        BEFORE the network fetch — bandwidth is fully saved.

      Position: must precede the app-embed <script> tags, which start at line
      ~8279 of the rendered HTML. Placing the meta tag right after
      <meta charset> gives it the earliest position that still respects the
      character-encoding-first ordering convention.

      Existing Shopify HTTP-header CSP (verified 2026-04-27 via curl -I):
        block-all-mixed-content; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests;
      Multiple CSPs are AND-ed; this meta tightens script-src without conflict.

      ALLOWLIST RATIONALE (kept apps audited from rendered HTML inventory):
        'self'                  — first-party theme assets (/cdn/shop/t/...);
                                  also incidentally allows /apps/apploy/...
                                  proxy script (~38 KB; Apploy banner is
                                  CSS-hidden so the script is inert anyway).
        'unsafe-inline'         — ~25 inline <script> blocks on home-v2 (GTM
                                  bootstrap, Hotjar, Klaviyo learnq, slideout
                                  drawer, FAQ, video lazy, Pandectes config,
                                  UpPromote tracking, MNTN pixel, TripleWhale,
                                  monkey-patch above, etc.). Nonce-ing all of
                                  them would be a large refactor; not justified.
        'unsafe-eval'           — GTM uses new Function() for tag templates.
        cdn.shopify.com/extensions/019dd854-…/  — UpPromote (Affiliate by
                                                  Secomapp). UUID-pinned so
                                                  the path-prefix excludes
                                                  every other extension UUID.
        cdn.shopify.com/extensions/019dcf35-…/  — Pandectes GDPR. Same.
        static.klaviyo.com      — Klaviyo main loader (signup_forms popup is
                                  blocked separately by appendChild patch above)
        *.hotjar.com            — static.hotjar.com loader + script.hotjar.com
                                  runtime + insights subdomain
        www.googletagmanager.com — GTM container
        www.google-analytics.com — GA4
        *.config-security.com   — TripleWhale (api. + conf. subdomains)
        *.mountain.com          — MNTN (dx.mountain.com pixel injector)

      OMITTED (verified not used on home-v2):
        cdn-widgetsrepository.yotpo.com — Yotpo (blocked)
        cdn.jsdelivr.net                — only Bevy used it (blocked)
        *.uppromote.com / *.cloudfront.net — UpPromote on home-v2 loads
                                              entirely from cdn.shopify.com
                                              extensions path; no cloudfront
        cdn.shopify.com/shopifycloud/   — no Shopify pixel infra on home-v2
                                          (verified via grep on rendered HTML)

      ROLLBACK: revert this meta tag if a kept-app integration breaks. CSP
      violation reports will appear in DevTools console with the blocked URL.

      Wave C Part 2 (2026-04-29) — added `style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'
      https://fonts.googleapis.com` directive to block the Atomato app embed's
      app.min.css (~3.7 KB gz, parser-injected, render-blocking ~730 ms per
      Lighthouse). Atomato JS is already script-src-blocked (UUID 019d9c07-…
      not in allowlist); its CSS targets a placeholder DIV that JS would have
      populated, so the CSS styled nothing visible. style-src enumeration
      audited 2026-04-29: 3 stylesheet origins on home-v2 (fonts.googleapis.com,
      ninjatransfers.com via 'self', and Atomato via cdn.shopify.com/extensions/
      — only the last gets blocked).
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' https://cdn.shopify.com/extensions/019dd854-eacc-7d28-b8ef-23ba0eb1dd49/ https://cdn.shopify.com/extensions/019e2616-959f-7eda-8d74-decdf9754103/ https://*.klaviyo.com https://*.hotjar.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://www.googleadservices.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://*.config-security.com https://*.mountain.com https://connect.facebook.net https://bat.bing.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://*.klaviyo.com">
  {%- endif -%}

